      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Most ophthalmic zoster occurs in healthy people and ocular complications occur in 50%. The mainstay of ocular therapy is topical steroid, but careful follow-up and withdrawal are essential. The place of systemic steroid therapy and acyclovir in immunocompetent patients with zoster is uncertain."},
